      <details class="fold" id="tool-noting">
        <summary><span class="fold-in">Deconstructing anxiety</span></summary>
        <p class="body">A simple, powerful mindfulness practice that doubles as a method for working with anxiety.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><span class="mk">1</span><div><p>Let your attention float freely.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="mk">2</span><div><p>As it drifts, various sights, sounds, sensations, and thoughts may grab your attention and stand out.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="mk">3</span><div><p>As this happens, notice whatever stands out most, and give it a light mental label:</p></div></li>
        </ol>
        <ul class="labels">
          <li><b>“Seeing”</b><span>for sights</span></li>
          <li><b>“Hearing”</b><span>for sounds</span></li>
          <li><b>“Feeling”</b><span>for physical sensations</span></li>
          <li><b>“Thinking”</b><span>for anything mental</span></li>
          <li><b>“Don’t know”</b><span>when you’re not sure what’s standing out</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="why2">
          <p>It’s accessible even when the mind is agitated or unable to focus.</p>
          <p>It’s well suited to short bursts of on-the-go practice.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="body">Use it any time you feel anxious or overwhelmed, like before:</p>
        <ul class="chips occasions"><li>Depositions</li><li>Court appearances</li><li>Client pitches</li><li>Business development opportunities</li><li>High-pressure calls or meetings</li></ul>
      </details>

      <details class="fold" id="tool-sleep">
        <summary><span class="fold-in">Getting to sleep</span></summary>
        <div class="why2">
          <p>As with anxiety, resisting sleeplessness only exacerbates it.</p>
          <p>Being less concerned with falling asleep will help you sleep better, and you can’t will yourself to become sleepy.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="body">So use the half-hour rule:</p>
        <ol class="cycle">
          <li>If you’re not falling asleep, don’t lie there and “keep trying.” It will only stress you.</li>
          <li>After roughly 20 to 30 minutes (don’t watch a clock), get up.</li>
          <li>Go into a different room, do something relaxing for 20 to 30 minutes, then go back to bed.</li>
          <li>If you become sleepy, great. If not, don’t worry about it. Just repeat the process as many times as you need.</li>
        </ol>
        <svg class="loop" viewBox="0 0 600 40" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M585 4 V22 Q585 34 573 34 H27 Q15 34 15 22 V10"/><path d="M8 14 L15 4 L22 14"/></svg>
        <p class="remember"><b>Remember:</b> missing sleep is very common and isn’t a big deal.</p>
      </details>

